      "final_text_tail": "Everything works correctly. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added flexible parsing for `dspy.ToolCalls` by implementing a `validate_input` model validator (`dspy/adapters/types/tool.py:266`) that normalizes varied LM output formats into the canonical `{\"tool_calls\": [...]}` structure:\n\n1. **Single-object normalization** \u2014 a dict with `name`/`args` (no `tool_calls` key) gets wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": [<obj>]}`\n2. **List normalization** \u2014 a bare list of tool-call dicts gets wrapped into `{\"tool_calls\": <list>}`\n3. **Canonical format preserved** \u2014 a dict already containing `tool_calls` passes through as-is\n4. **JSON strings** are parsed first, then normalized; non-JSON strings (or JSON that fails to parse) are returned unchanged\n\nThis follows the same `@pydantic.model_validator(mode=\"before\")` pattern already used by `dspy.Code` and `dspy.Image`, so it fires automatically during pydantic validation. The existing 26 `test_tool.py` tests and 42 JSON/chat adapter tests all still pass.",
